      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup / Instructions\n1. Connect your Telegram bot and Google Sheets OAuth2 credentials (DeepSeek credential is also required).\n2. Questions sheet: id, question, model_answer. Question IDs must be consecutive integers starting at 1.\n3. Student State sheet (gid=0 in the configured state spreadsheet): user_id, current_q, answers, started_at, total_questions, max_score. Keep user_id unique.\n4. Results sheet: user_id, total_score, percentage, feedback, evaluated_at, total_questions, max_score, name, username, answers_json. Add a column with the exact header answers_json to Results before activating.\n5. Verify the two configured spreadsheet IDs and sheet tabs match your account. The workflow upserts only the current user's state; it does not clear other students' rows.\n6. For heavy public traffic, use a transactional database and a queue; Google Sheets has API quotas and is not an atomic per-user lock.",
